16","derivedTextPath":"state/research/upper-legion-color/de-laurence-1916-normalized-text.txt","startCodePoint":42887,"endCodePointExclusive":43187},"sourceRefs":["public:goetia_de_laurence_1916"],"assertionLayer":"source-assertion","id":"systems:goetic-upper:16","viewIds":["catalogue:de-laurence-1916"]},{"witnessId":"de-laurence-1916","source":"goetic-upper:de-laurence-1916:Amaymon","target":"de-laurence-1916:chief:70","type":"source-reported-power-over","sourceMeaning":"Seere under Amaymon in the chief70 passage; do not transfer this direction across different witnesses.","evidence":{"text":" Seere , Sear , or Seir .—The Seventieth Spirit is Seere, Sear, or Seir. He is a Mighty Prince, and Powerful, under Amaymon , King of the East. He appeareth in the Form of a Beautiful Man, riding upon a Winged Horse. His Office is to go and come; and to bring ab","sourceId":"public:goetia_de_laurence_1916","derivedTextPath":"state/research/upper-legion-color/de-laurence-1916-normalized-text.txt","startCodePoint":64171,"endCodePointExclusive":64433},"sourceRefs":["public:goetia_de_laurence_1916"],"assertionLayer":"source-assertion","id":"systems:goetic-upper:17","viewIds":["catalogue:de-laurence-1916"]},{"source":"peterson-sloane3825:rank:editorial87:0","target":"peterson-sloane3825:chief:1","type":"has-editorially-listed-rank-member","witnessId":"peterson-sloane3825","sourceRefs":["public:goetia_peterson_sloane3825"],"assertionLayer":"source-assertion","sourceRole":"modern editorial note87","evidence":{"sourceId":"public:goetia_peterson_sloane3825","derivedTextPath":"state/research/upper-legion-color/peterson-sloane3825-normalized-text.txt","startCodePoint":60553,"endCodePointExclusive":60662,"text":"Kings (8): Bael, Paimon, Beleth, Purson, Asmoday, Vine (King & Earl), Balam, Zagan (King & President), Belial"},"id":"systems:goetic-upper:18","viewIds":["catalogue:peterson-sloane3825"]},{"source":"peterson-sloane3825:rank:editorial87:0","target":"peterson-sloane3825:chief:9","ty